  "verbalization": "Neogitogenin appears to share a common pathway of interaction with SNB-78 through multiple indirect routes. The first pathway links Neogitogenin to CAKI-2, which is targeted by Pseudoaeruginosin KT554, and then to SNB-78. The second pathway connects Neogitogenin to Solute carrier family 22 member 7, which is targeted by Isoderrone, also leading to SNB-78. The third pathway links Neogitogenin to CAKI-2 again, which is targeted by Acetyldeschloroelatol, also leading to SNB-78. These findings suggest that Neogitogenin may act as a modulator of SNB-78 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly by interacting with various targets in the same biological pathway. The evidence supports a potential role for Neogitogenin in influencing SNB-78 through a network of downstream targets, highlighting a complex, multi-tiered interaction that may involve overlapping pathways or functional redundancies.",
